    # - When k = 1, answer is n (any single planet)

    # For general case, the number of valid sequences is:
    # n * (n-1) * ... * (n-k+1) when movement constraints allow freedom

    # The result is n! / (n-k)! = P(n, k) = nPrk
    # (permutations of k items from n)

